=== group Z: zero stays zero -- 'nothing ran' must not become 'passed' ===
  ok       Z1 a log with no summary at all is 0 ran, never a pass
  ok       Z2 an empty log is 0 ran
  ok       Z3 'Ran 0 checks, all passed' -> 0 ran (the __main__-guard shape, shell edition)
  ok       Z4 '0 passed, 0 failed' -> 0 ran, so a suite that collected nothing cannot pass
  ok       Z5 '===== 0 check(s): 0 ok, 0 FAILED =====' -> 0 ran
  ok       Z6 a check whose NAME quotes a summary is output, not a summary
  ok       Z7 the LAST summary wins, as tail -1 did (5 passed + 1 failed = 6 ran)

=== group V: the verdict branch order, so ran=0 keeps its own answer ===
  ok       V1 rc!=0 is FAIL-RC even with a green summary
  ok       V2 a skip outranks the zero count, so a skipping suite is not 'no tests ran'
  ok       V3 rc=0 and nothing collected is NO-TESTS-RAN, NOT a pass
  ok       V4 rc=0 over a summary that names failures is FAIL-CHECKS
  ok       V5 rc=0, checks ran, none failed, none skipped is the only PASS
  ok       V6 NO-TESTS-RAN and PASS are different tokens (the distinction is the point)

=== group W: the driver still counts every non-PASS verdict as a failure ===
  ok       W  the FAIL-RC arm increments FAILURES
  ok       W  the FAIL-SKIP arm increments FAILURES
  ok       W  the NO-TESTS-RAN arm increments FAILURES
  ok       W  the FAIL-CHECKS arm increments FAILURES

